  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 3, 'Planning and implementing a digital health enterprise: phases, steps and resources'. Seven numbered phases, each with its steps: 01 assessing the current state and enabling environment; 02 establishing a shared understanding and strategic planning; 03 defining the future state; 04 planning the enterprise architecture; 05 determining health content requirements; 06 M&E of digital health implementations and fostering data use; 07 implementing, maintaining and scaling. Beside them a grid of tiles names resources for each phase, marked as PDF for print or online environment; among them the WHO-ITU national eHealth strategy toolkit, the Digital implementation investment guide (DIIG), WHO guideline recommendations on digital interventions, Open Health Information Exchange, TOGAF, and a highlighted tile 'WHO SMART guidelines: digital adaptation kits (this document) and machine-readable recommendations' in phase 05. Source: adapted from WHO (reference 1).",
